### v0.3.0 Decision Notes
- Draft example command
```ptt
/file roadmap.txt :ai claude Add the green button class from phase 1 to the stylesheet, only output the code. :r styles.css :s \
/persist styles.css :ss /print "Ruh-Roh!"
```
#### Thoughts on syntax:
- /command must be on newlines always.
- Commands are always command -> input -> params
- :command / operators only use the preceding output as input
- No globbing or loops to start with - don't want variables or list iteration or arrays or all the BASH boggins just yet.
- That kind of scripting can be done via combination of actual shell and the -c flag.

